WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.862
So, the decisions and the next steps.

2
00:00:02.862 --> 00:00:08.320
First, the sponsor and CIO authorize
one authoritative DDI policy plane,

3
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:13.413
and the DNS/DDI team settles Book
08's five configuration decisions

4
00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:18.962
within 90 days and reports the residual
risk to the authorizing official.

5
00:00:18.962 --> 00:00:20.325
That's the book's ask.

6
00:00:20.325 --> 00:00:26.247
Second, write the requirement as capabilities,
each mapped to the rule behind it:

7
00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:31.183
signing and validation, encrypted
DNS, Protective DNS forwarding,

8
00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:34.862
discovery and inventory,
IPv6, logging retention.

9
00:00:34.862 --> 00:00:38.800
No rule names a product, so the
solicitation shouldn't either.

10
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.823
Third, request the same evidence
pack from every candidate:

11
00:00:42.823 --> 00:00:47.092
the FedRAMP listing and exactly
what its scope covers, the STIG,

12
00:00:47.092 --> 00:00:51.854
an active FIPS 140-3 certificate,
Common Criteria status, the advisory

13
00:00:51.854 --> 00:00:56.862
response commitment, and a three-to-five-year
cost on the same assumptions.

14
00:00:56.862 --> 00:00:59.000
Record every gap with an owner.

15
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.254
Fourth, choose a delegation
pattern for each division,

16
00:01:02.254 --> 00:01:06.594
write down what stays central, and
pilot it with one division, ideally one

17
00:01:06.594 --> 00:01:11.150
with overlapping address space, because
that's where the design gets tested.

18
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:15.449
Fifth, the CISO sizes logging
to M-26-14's retention,

19
00:01:15.449 --> 00:01:19.850
and tests it at peak query
rates and with the SIEM down.

20
00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.763
The next step needs no award.

21
00:01:21.763 --> 00:01:26.386
List every DNS, DHCP and IPAM
requirement your systems inherit,

22
00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:30.838
the capability each needs, and
the evidence that would prove it.

23
00:01:30.838 --> 00:01:35.338
Book 08 has the detail,
with every claim footnoted.

24
00:01:35.338 --> 00:01:36.170
Thank you.
